# Subproject dependencies (managed by the wrap mechanism, not committed).
#
# Deny-by-default (#1814).  Meson extracts each wrap into
# subprojects/<directory>, where <directory> is the wrap's `directory =`
# value or, absent that key, the wrap's own name -- so the name changes on
# every version bump.  Naming the extracted directories one by one
# desynchronised at 8ab99d14, which bumped xxhash.wrap to 0.8.4 and left the
# rule at 0.8.3, and every worktree stayed permanently dirty for several
# releases.  Nothing objected because nothing compared the rule against the
# wrap.
#
# Enumerating names cannot be made safe: meson also creates
# subprojects/packagecache, which is neither a wrap name nor any `directory =`
# value (mesonbuild/wrap/wrap.py:377).  So ignore everything directly under
# subprojects/ and re-include the tracked inputs by name.
#
# `subprojects/*` carries an internal slash, so git anchors it here and `*`
# does not cross `/`: it matches the direct children only, not any depth.
# `*` does match a leading dot, so .wraplock needs its own re-inclusion.
# scripts/ci/check-subprojects-ignored.sh asserts both halves.
#
# To track a NEW file directly under subprojects/, add a "!" line below.
# Without one, `git add <path>` refuses it by name and `git add -A` drops it
# with no message at all.
subprojects/*
!subprojects/*.wrap
!subprojects/.wraplock
!subprojects/packagefiles/

*.uncrustify

# SBOM generation artifacts (timestamped, regenerated per release; only snapshot.txt committed)
sbom/*.spdx.json
sbom/*.cdx.json

# Issue #1570: ci-run-telemetry.py writes saved API responses and generated
# reports here.  Measurement output, never source.
/ci-telemetry/
